1. `ofElement(PublicClass)` -> PUBLIC. min(PUBLIC, PUBLIC) -> PUBLIC.
2. `getEnclosingElement()` -> `VisibilityTest`. `ofElement(VisibilityTest)` -> PUBLIC. min(PUBLIC, PUBLIC) -> PUBLIC.
3. `getEnclosingElement()` -> `com.google.auto.common` (Package). `ofElement(Package)` -> PUBLIC. min(PUBLIC, PUBLIC) -> PUBLIC.
4. `getEnclosingElement()` -> null (or module?).

If running in Java 11 environment, maybe the `PackageElement` is enclosed in a `ModuleElement`? 

If `currentElement` becomes a `ModuleElement`, `ofElement` will fall through to `DEFAULT` because modules don't have PUBLIC modifier (they have `open` etc, but `Modifier.PUBLIC` might not be present or applicable in the way this code expects).

